// Brought to u by MidManStudio
//
// Docs only: stage 1 of decision D10 (a MID function that allocates outside `with arena` takes its caller's arena), chat 10.
// 8 anchored edits over 4 files (docs/LLVM_POC.md, docs/LLVM_ROADMAP.md, docs/LLVM_BACKEND_STATUS.md, docs/ARENA_STRINGS.md);
// each anchor occurs exactly once and none is a whole line. This overwrites the earlier patch.mdix, which is right only because
// that one (AS4a, from the other chat) is applied on master: check that before running this. Independent of the tarball
// ubel-llvm-zmid-17.tar.gz: apply them in either order.

@CONFIG(
  version    -> "1.0.0",
  author     -> "MidManStudio",
  features   -> "quickfuncs,data",
  debug_mode -> "off"
)

@QUICKFUNCS(
  ~patch_replace_text<object>(_path, _anchor, _content) {
    return { path = _path, op = "replace_text", anchor = _anchor, content = _content }
  }
)

@DATA(
  patch_files::
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_POC.md", "| in a MID function outside `with arena` | **refused**: the language does not say where that allocates (MEMORY_MODEL.md, open decision 3)", "| in a MID function outside `with arena` | the caller's arena, through a hidden first parameter (decision D10, stage 1, provisional; see the paragraphs under this table)")
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_POC.md", "Field expressions are evaluated first, in source order, then the object", "**A MID function outside `with arena` (decision D10, stage 1, provisional, chat 10).** The row above no longer refuses. A `@tier(mid)` function that allocates outside any `with arena` of its own, or that calls such a function from there, takes a hidden first parameter `ptr %arena.in`, the arena of its caller. Inside `with arena` a call passes the innermost open arena; outside one, a function passes on the arena it was given, and a call from a place with no arena at all (a HIGH function, `main`) is refused with the callee's name. The parameter is not on the function's own arena stack, so `return`, `break` and `continue` destroy only the arenas the function opened. Which functions take it is found by emitting to a fixed point: `emit_program` runs `emit_pass` with the set found so far and repeats until no function is added, so the emitter itself is the judge of what allocates and there is no second walk over the syntax tree. The caller marks the arena scannable whenever it passes it on, because the callee may store pointers to GC objects in it. Still refused: `main`, the body of a closure (it does not hold the arena), an interpolated string (sema tags it with its arena only inside a lexical `with arena`) and LOW code. Wherever an earlier section here says that something is refused in MID outside `with arena`, read: allowed in a function that takes the caller's arena, except for those cases. Strings built with `+` or a method, lists, `for` over a list and boxed optionals still live in the GC heap, as they do inside `with arena`.\n\n**Known hole (D1 v2).** Sema does not tag the result of a call to such a function, so an arena value can leave its block through one. A function that builds a struct, called inside a nested `with arena` and assigned to a variable declared outside that block, is accepted; the same escape written as a struct literal in the block is rejected (TIER-004). The accepted program reads an arena that has been destroyed (it printed the expected number in a test, which proves nothing). Closing it is D1 v2: tag the result with the region of the arena the call was given. Until then it is a gap that only programs that did not compile before can reach.\n\nField expressions are evaluated first, in source order, then the object")
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_POC.md", "the number that tests Ubel's central claim. Open.", "the number that tests Ubel's central claim. Built as stage 1 of D10 in chat 10 (provisional); see the paragraphs under the struct table in Tier lowering. With it `binarytrees_arena` builds natively. Its first sandbox number was 5.2x of Rust and no faster than Ubel HIGH: 1.9 s of 2.6 s were system time, 820,635 page faults, because every `with arena(512MB)` round maps a fresh chunk and unmaps it at the end. Retaining one big chunk in the runtime (tried, not delivered) took the run to 0.40 s with 12,362 faults, close to Rust here. Whether to adopt that retention is open (LANGBENCH.md, Ubel MID in the sandbox).")
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_POC.md", "- 2026-11-24 (chat 10): **First benchmarks on a GitHub-hosted runner.**", "- 2026-11-25 (chat 10): **Stage 1 of D10: a MID function that allocates outside `with arena` takes its caller's arena.** The owner chose to build stage 1 (a hybrid with the hidden parameter as the default; all provisional). `emit.rs`: such a function gets a hidden first parameter `ptr %arena.in`, kept off the function's arena stack so `return`, `break` and `continue` destroy only the arenas it opened; a call passes the innermost open arena, or this function's own when none is open; a call with no arena at all (from HIGH, from `main`) is refused with the callee's name; the caller marks the arena scannable whenever it passes it on. Which functions take it is found by emitting to a fixed point (`emit_program` repeats `emit_pass` until the set stops growing). Allowed there now: structs, enum payloads, capturing closures, string `+` and builds by method, lists, `for` over a list and boxed optionals. Still refused: `main`, a closure body, an interpolated string, LOW. Fixtures 55 to 59 (equal to the interpreter), `u_mid_main_arena`, `u_mid_closure_body`, and the five old outside-`with arena` refusals re-aimed (a HIGH caller with no arena). `binarytrees_arena.ubl` builds natively. Verified on a fresh clone of master 603fef8 with the tarball applied by the real applier: core lib 232, ubel_llvm 6 unit and 19 integration, doc-tests ok; `run_equiv.sh` 138 passed, 0 failed at 64-bit and with `-m32`; `run_ubel_build.sh` with the committed tables: 73 supported programs equal `ubel run`, 58 intentional refusals, 214 `err_` rejected, 32 of 201 `ok_` built (the same as before, so no `ok_` fixture is newly unlocked); GC stress 1 with ASan and UBSan on fixtures 55 to 59 and the list, optional and arena-scan examples; langbench `--size small`: every installed language correct, ubel-mid included. Mutation testing by hand, 19 mutants of the new code: 17 caught at once; one survivor is equivalent (passing the outermost instead of the innermost arena changes where an object lives, which no output shows); one (no scan mark at the call site) survived the first fixture 58, which was rewritten (the callee builds the string, 1,500,000 churn iterations) and now catches it in a normal run at -O0 and -O2. Known hole: sema does not tag the result of such a call (D1 v2), so an arena value can leave its block through one; see Tier lowering. Finding: the first sandbox number for the arena benchmark was 5.2x of Rust and no faster than Ubel HIGH, with 1.9 s of 2.6 s in the kernel (820,635 page faults from a fresh 512 MB chunk per round); retaining one big chunk took it to 0.40 s (experiment, not delivered; see LANGBENCH.md). Not verified: the hosted runner, ARM, macOS, Termux, the Go, C#, Zig and Odin rows (not installed in this sandbox).\n- 2026-11-24 (chat 10): **First benchmarks on a GitHub-hosted runner.**")
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_ROADMAP.md", "First stage proposed, not started: the hidden parameter for arenas only, resolved statically in the emitter.", "First stage BUILT in chat 10 (provisional): the hidden parameter for arenas only, resolved statically in the emitter and found by emitting to a fixed point. Known hole: sema does not tag the result of a call to such a function (D1 v2), so an arena value can escape its block through one (docs/LLVM_POC.md, Tier lowering).")
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_ROADMAP.md", "It would also settle every refusal that says where it allocates is not decided yet (structs, enums, strings, and lists in arenas).", "It settled the refusals that said where it allocates is not decided yet for structs, enum payloads, closure objects, string `+` and methods, lists and boxed optionals (lists themselves still live in the GC heap); an interpolated string, a closure body and `main` stay refused.")
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_BACKEND_STATUS.md", "building a string or a struct in MID outside `with arena` (decision open)", "an interpolated string, a closure body or `main` allocating in MID outside `with arena` (the rest is stage 1 of D10, provisional)")
    patch_replace_text("docs/ARENA_STRINGS.md", "refused in LOW and in MID outside `with arena`.", "refused in LOW; in MID outside `with arena` it is allowed only in a function that takes its caller's arena (D10, stage 1).")
)
